# Step files of vm/live-smoke.d/ that have no recording in this directory yet:
# one token per line, the step file's own name without .sh.  A file is in this
# list or it has a <flavor>-...-replay.txt here, never both and never neither --
# tests/test_live_smoke.py (R31) is what says so, and vm/live-smoke.d/
# selftest-offline.sh repeats the check in the shell.
#
# A recording is made by booting that flavor's golden once and running
# vm/live-smoke.d/guest-capture.sh in it; on this host that is one VM at a time,
# which is why the list is not empty.  The batch that first runs a flavor
# deletes its own line here in the same commit that adds the recording.

# A second class of line arrived with the X11 proxy: `proxy:<flavor>`, one per
# FLAVOR rather than per step file, for the `proxy` phase vm/live-smoke.d/
# common.sh added after `wm` on every Wayland step file.  It is per flavor
# because what that phase measures is per compositor AND per distribution -- the
# original xdotool is 3.20211022.1 on Ubuntu and Fedora and 4.20260303.1 on Arch
# -- so a recording on one says nothing about the others.  Every flavor whose
# `# vmctl-desktop:` names a Wayland step file is listed here until its `proxy`
# phase has been run; the run that records one deletes its own line in the same
# commit that adds the recording.  resolute-sway was the first, on 2026-09-11:
# 27 pass, 0 fail, recorded as resolute-sway-1.11-windows-wm-proxy-replay.txt.
